13. Explore vs Exploit

The Metamap should not always choose the best-known route.

Define:

\Pi_t=
\begin{cases}
\text{known high-value strategy}, & \text{exploit}\\
\text{novel plausible strategy}, & \text{explore}
\end{cases}

Exploration probability may increase when:

* uncertainty is high,
* known routes perform poorly,
* the problem is structurally novel,
* a new Seal or portal requires testing.

Exploration should decrease when:

* stakes are high,
* a validated strategy exists,
* budget is constrained,
* novelty has low expected value.

