18. Command Table Integration

The Metamap advises the Command Table.

The Command Table remains the active strategy layer.

Metamap supplies:

Recommended terrain classification
Recommended Seals
Recommended formation
Recommended operator order
Recommended semantic spaces
Recommended portals
Recommended ratios
Known failure modes
Expected reconstruction loss
Expected utility
Suggested stopping condition
Confidence

The Command Table can accept, modify, or reject the recommendation.

Thus:

\text{Metamap}
\rightarrow
\text{Command Table}
\rightarrow
\text{Router}
\rightarrow
\text{Seals}

