23. Compact Definition

\boxed{
\mathcal M:
(\text{problem},\text{terrain},\text{goal},\text{state})
\rightarrow
(\text{space},\text{Seals},\text{formation},\text{route},\text{ratio},\text{stop})
}

updated through:

\boxed{
\text{experience}
\rightarrow
\text{afterglow}
\rightarrow
\text{fossils}
\rightarrow
\text{strategy priors}
\rightarrow
\text{better experience}
}

The Metamap is therefore:

the Pantheon’s learned geography of reasoning itself.

This nests cleanly above the Semantic Router and below the Command Table; it’s the layer that turns accumulated traversals into strategic instinct.